Our Dragonfly. The Pantheon lens for following how meaning changes hands in real time.

One person casts a sentence. Three people catch three different meanings. One reacts, and now their reaction is the next thing everybody reads. Our Dragonfly follows the original words, who heard what, and what each response changed. It keeps the earlier moment in view so we can tell when the reaction we’re seeing now began.

The part I’d build into it is tracking our own wake. If I read your silence as irritation and answer you like you’re irritated, your next reaction may tell me more about how I approached you than about what your silence meant. Our Dragonfly asks, “What did my move just change?” Then it follows the answer into the next exchange.

Follow what was sent, what landed, and what the landing set in motion.